        {
          "id": 750067467,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "On the welcome screen, double-clicking on en0 starts a capture, but double-clicking on ciscodump pops up a dialog.  Perhaps that's because it requires a parameter.\n\nOn the Capture Options screen, double-clicking on en0 does *not* start a capture.\n\nAnd, for what it's worth, with Wireshark build from the tip of the master branch on Ubuntu 20.04, double-clicking on ens33 does *not* start a capture, so not starting a capture when you double-clock an interface in the Capture Options dialog is *not* macOS-only.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
